{
  "_id": "pnSnfmB2iVRIzSFO",
  "name": "Know-It-All",
  "type": "feat",
  "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-open-purple.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<blockquote><p><em>There is no subject on which you lack an opinion, and irritatingly, you are usually right. Locks, languages, lineages, poisons, the tensile strength of a rope bridge: you have read about all of it, and you will explain it now whether or not anyone asked.</em></p></blockquote>\n<p><strong>1st Level</strong></p><ul><li>You do not gain Skill Increases. Instead you are Expert in all non-Lore skills.<ul><li>Lore skills from your background match these ranks.</li></ul></li><li>You gain two extra Skill Feats every level.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>5th Level</strong></p><ul><li>Once per turn, you may Recall Knowledge as a free action.</li><li>When you Recall Knowledge, treat a success as a critical success.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>7th Level</strong></p><ul><li>Master in all non-Lore skills.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>15th Level</strong></p><ul><li>Legendary in all non-Lore skills.</li></ul>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>In Foundry:</strong> every non-Lore skill is at least Expert, Master from 7th and Legendary from 15th. A <em>Know-It-All</em> feat group with two skill feat slots per level appears on your Feats tab. From 5th a Recall Knowledge success is a critical success on the roll.</p>\n<p>For the table: do not spend your class's skill increases; raise your background Lore skills to match by hand; and Recall Knowledge as a free action once per turn.</p>",
      "gm": ""
    },
    "publication": {
      "title": "Ascendant: Mythic Rebuilt",
      "authors": "",
      "license": "ORC",
      "remaster": true
    },
